summary.value:
This paper targets the task of Video Temporal Grounding (VTG) and proposes the causal-inference framework CausalVTG. The method has three key components:
1.Causality-Aware Disentangled Encoder (CADE) based on front-door adjustment to eliminate confounding bias between visual and textual modalities;
2.Multi-Scale Temporal Perception (MSTP) to adaptively capture actions of different temporal lengths;
3.Counterfactual Contrastive Learning to judge whether a query can truly be grounded.
The unified model simultaneously addresses Moment Retrieval, Highlight Detection, and Query Relevance. It achieves state-of-the-art results on five benchmarks—QVHighlights, Charades-STA, ActivityNet-Caption, Charades-RF, and ActivityNet-RF—showing especially strong performance under strict IoU thresholds and in “false-query” scenarios.

